// A `mut` binding to an empty literal is exempt from E0023 only so an accumulator's later writes
// can supply its element type. With no such write, the type stays an undeterminable hole — the
// `mut` analogue of the immutable error, fixable by an annotation (`mut acc: List<int> = []`) or a
// later assignment. The checker is shared, so both backends agree.
// expect: error E0023 at 7:11
// expect: exit 1
mut acc = [];
echo acc;
